00:54:13.820 --> 00:54:16.410
that I have back to my NAS box.

00:54:20.720 --> 00:54:22.835
And of course some
other information

00:54:22.835 --> 00:54:23.710
about the networking.

00:54:31.580 --> 00:54:35.790
If I were to-- if
there were nodes--

00:54:35.790 --> 00:54:38.360
say I had to expand
my existing cluster,

00:54:38.360 --> 00:54:40.660
whether it's a
virtual or bare metal,

00:54:40.660 --> 00:54:45.450
it would show the
lists of FXT nodes

00:54:45.450 --> 00:54:46.930
that were waiting
to join in here.

00:54:46.930 --> 00:54:49.910
So this is how easy it
is to actually spin up

00:54:49.910 --> 00:54:51.590
another Avere cluster.

00:54:51.590 --> 00:54:55.566
And actually, we'll see if we
can-- not sure how long this

00:54:55.566 --> 00:54:58.010
is going to take to boot
up, but nonetheless, it'll

00:54:58.010 --> 00:55:00.070
be fun to see if we can do this.

00:55:00.070 --> 00:55:04.240
I'm just spinning up another
virtual machine here.

00:55:04.240 --> 00:55:06.590
And while that's
coming up, we'll

00:55:06.590 --> 00:55:10.670
move around to- we'll step
through this a little bit more.

00:55:10.670 --> 00:55:13.780
So this is my Vserver
that I have created.

00:55:13.780 --> 00:55:16.460
I've named it Avere-GNS.

00:55:16.460 --> 00:55:19.440
All right, there it is there.

00:55:19.440 --> 00:55:21.484
I can hit this to
create a new one,

00:55:21.484 --> 00:55:23.400
or I can suspend this
one for whatever reason,

00:55:23.400 --> 00:55:24.850
or I can remove this.

00:55:24.850 --> 00:55:26.730
So I want to just get
rid of the cluster,

00:55:26.730 --> 00:55:31.150
or for whatever reason, I don't
have that NAS, that core filer,

00:55:31.150 --> 00:55:33.440
I need to remove the
virtual server first.

00:55:33.440 --> 00:55:36.960
And then I need to remove
the core filer second.

00:55:36.960 --> 00:55:41.147
This is just details
for that virtual server.

00:55:41.147 --> 00:55:42.730
The namespace is
something else that's

00:55:42.730 --> 00:55:47.286
probably actually one of
the more interesting pieces

00:55:47.286 --> 00:55:48.410
that you need to deal with.

00:55:48.410 --> 00:55:50.410
So in order-- I mentioned
this before-- in order

00:55:50.410 --> 00:55:52.797
to create a virtual server
and have it represented,

00:55:52.797 --> 00:55:54.630
I have to have a junction
point to represent

00:55:54.630 --> 00:55:59.300
those exports or that
bucket or container

00:55:59.300 --> 00:56:01.570
from an object storage device.

00:56:01.570 --> 00:56:03.800
So this is what I've done here.

00:56:03.800 --> 00:56:07.230
I've actually created
the namespace with /vol.

00:56:07.230 --> 00:56:10.030
I could call it whatever.

00:56:10.030 --> 00:56:11.360
I can add a new junction here.

00:56:14.740 --> 00:56:15.730
Let's call it vol2.

00:56:15.730 --> 00:56:18.130
And I know that because
I know that there's

00:56:18.130 --> 00:56:21.990
another export from my NAS box.

00:56:21.990 --> 00:56:26.670
I'm just defining
the core filer here.

00:56:26.670 --> 00:56:29.605
And if you have a
number of exports,

00:56:29.605 --> 00:56:31.560
it's going to show
up in this list here.

00:56:31.560 --> 00:56:35.896
So I already have a
junction point for vol1.

00:56:35.896 --> 00:56:37.270
I'm going to create
one for vol2.

00:56:37.270 --> 00:56:40.700
And then I'm going
to submit that.

00:56:40.700 --> 00:56:43.520
OK, so now I have two
different directors

00:56:43.520 --> 00:56:46.610
under the top level,
vol1 and vol2.

00:56:49.760 --> 00:56:51.850
And I could potentially
just go ahead

00:56:51.850 --> 00:56:56.130
and mount that from a
client without any problem.

00:56:56.130 --> 00:56:59.020
This is where I change my export
policies if I need to do that.

00:56:59.020 --> 00:56:59.820
You probably would.

00:57:05.100 --> 00:57:08.460
This is where we
create the rules.

00:57:08.460 --> 00:57:10.840
Once I create the policies,
I would apply those.

00:57:15.122 --> 00:57:16.830
So for SMB, I would
want to go into here.

00:57:16.830 --> 00:57:21.160
There's a few other
modifications and settings

00:57:21.160 --> 00:57:24.922
