01:32:27.140 --> 01:32:29.019
So that definitely happens.

01:32:29.019 --> 01:32:30.560
The majority of
customers I work with

01:32:30.560 --> 01:32:32.680
are doing an offline transcode.

01:32:32.680 --> 01:32:34.180
And that's super easy to do.

01:32:34.180 --> 01:32:36.030
The real time, as
you know, latency

01:32:36.030 --> 01:32:38.070
does play, and the question
of how many seconds

01:32:38.070 --> 01:32:42.630
do you want between ingest
and push up to the CDN.

01:32:42.630 --> 01:32:45.150
The other questions include,
are you pushing to your prem,

01:32:45.150 --> 01:32:46.650
and then you're doing a
distribution from there

01:32:46.650 --> 01:32:47.340
locally?

01:32:47.340 --> 01:32:52.600
Or using Fastly or we have
a variety of partners.

01:32:52.600 --> 01:32:54.030
We also have our
own CDN as well,

01:32:54.030 --> 01:32:55.876
so happy to talk with
you more about that.

01:32:55.876 --> 01:32:56.808
AUDIENCE: Thank you.

01:32:56.808 --> 01:32:59.610
JEFF KEMBER: Thanks.

